# orchestrator-desktop — Tauri + React

## Layout
```
src/
  api/           client.ts (IPC), types.ts (DTOs)
  ui/            App.tsx composition root; category folders (see ui/README.md)
  ui/docker/     Docker section (engine, containers, images, volumes)
src-tauri/src/
  main.rs        Tauri commands
  core_bridge.rs Java process, stdin/stdout IPC, core_event
  java_runtime.rs spawn core, PATH/JAVA_HOME
  java_env.rs    Java 17+ validation
```

## UI
`App.tsx` is the composition root at `src/ui/`. Primitives each own a kebab folder (`icons/Icons`, `modal`, `dropdown`, `tooltip`, `toast`, `resize-handle`). Shared menu items live in `src/ui/components/context-menu-items/`.

| Folder | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `components/context-menu-items/` | Shared menu items (`ContextMenuItems`) |
| `layout/` | Toolbar, status bar, import, services workspace chrome |
| `service-table/` | Service table owner plus row, context menu, tech/script metadata |
| `containers/` | Logical workspace containers (not Docker) |
| `logs/` | Service logs and multi-service monitor |
| `config/` | Preferences and Java runtime |
| `ports/` | Kill-port modal and listening ports |
| `workspace/` | Workspace bootstrap hooks and reorder helpers |
| `docker/docker/` | Real Docker engine, images, volumes |
| `docker/hooks/` | Docker data and action hooks |
| `icons/` | `Icons.tsx` plus SVG sets |

## IPC flow
React `api.*` → `invoke("core_request")` → CoreBridge → Java → response / log events via `useCoreEvents`.

Contract table: repo `docs/reference/IPC.md`. Integration flow: `docs/integration/INTEGRATION.md`.

## Rust notes
- `core_bridge`: single session mutex for request lifecycle; recv timeout is per-request (`timeoutSecs`, 5–360s) and kills JVM on expiry; one retry on shutdown/transport errors
- stdout reader: `read_until` + `from_utf8_lossy` (not line iterator)
- Core not started in Tauri `.setup`
- stderr trace: `ORCHESTRATOR_CORE_TRACE=1`, log file `desktop-logs/core.stderr.log`

## Dev commands
| Command | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Vite only |
| `npm run dev:full` | Maven JAR + Vite + tauri dev (same as `scripts/unix/start.sh`) |
| `npm run verify:core-ipc` | Smoke test against JAR |

`devUrl` must stay `http://127.0.0.1:5173`; Vite `--host 127.0.0.1`.

## Hooks
See `src/ui/README.md`. App.tsx uses `useWorkspaceData`, `useServiceFilters`, `useCoreEvents`, `useServiceBranchPolling`, `useServiceShortcuts`, `useJavaRuntime` from `ui/workspace/hooks` and `ui/service-table/hooks`.

## Top-level sections
`Toolbar` switches `AppSection` (`services` | `docker`). The services `<main>` stays mounted and is hidden via inline `display` so log subscriptions survive the switch; `DockerView` only fetches/polls when `active`.

## API client
- `core()` serializes IPC in a queue (Windows safety); optional per-call timeout (docker prune/remove use a longer one)
- Branch polling: `useServiceBranchPolling` + `listServiceBranches`
- Tauri-only: folder pickers, `get_runtime_settings`, `set_java_runtime_path`
- Auto-update: `tauri-plugin-updater` + aviso em `StatusBar`; manifesto `latest.json` na release GitHub

## Build
```bash
npm run build
cd src-tauri && cargo check
```

Full desktop bundle: `scripts/unix/build.sh` / `scripts/windows/build.ps1`.
